"about": "CNOSSOS-EU point-source test cases TC01-TC28 of ISO/TR 17534-4:2020, direct path only, as published by NoiseModelling. cut_points: every profile vertex projected on the horizontal source-receiver line (s_m from the source); ground_g applies from that vertex to the next. Walls are building/barrier edge crossings with their top altitude. Levels are for the case sound_power_db in every octave band (93 dB; TC28 150 dB), 10 C, 70 % RH. Compact layout: source/receiver are [x_m, y_m, z_m, z_ground_m]; cut_points rows are [type, s_m, z_ground_m, ground_g]; walls rows are [s_m, top_z_m, z_ground_m, intersection]; bands holds one row per case and octave band in band_columns order (null where the reference publishes no value; exp_LH/exp_LF are the NoiseModelling Java-test expectations, which differ from the JSON reference LH/LF in three cells). Every numeric literal is byte-identical to the transcribed reference.",
"reference_alpha_atm_db_per_km": [0.12, 0.41, 1.04, 1.93, 3.66, 9.66, 32.77, 116.88],
"p_favourable_for_L": 0.5,
